  "description": "The MULTISPORT 3 TREKKING bike has been slimmed down so much that the high-quality aluminium frame weighs just 1,590 grams. A clear sign that this hybrid bike can also meet athletic goals and get up to high speeds. The built-in gear mechanism is a Shimano XT Trekking, one of the highest-quality trekking component groups on the market. This set is known for its robustness, reliability, and durability, making it the first choice of commuters and touring riders alike. The MULTISPORT disk brakes are also from Shimano. Equipped with 180 mm rotors in front as well as 160 mm rotors in the back, the hydraulic Shimano XT Trekking disk brakes have a confident grip. You won’t need to worry about having enough braking power in wet conditions. Despite its agility, this model does not compromise on comfort – the RockShox Paragon Gold suspension fork with lockout expertly absorbs unevenness and unites first-class performance with design. The MULTISPORT rolls smoothly on its Schwalbe Marathon Racer tyres. The Racktime cargo rack with an integrated rear light and the 70 Lux B + M headlights provides safety in road traffic and make the MULTISPORT 3 perfectly suitable for daily use. * approx. 14.1 kg, may vary by up to +/- 5% due to manufacturing tolerances, weight for matt black/shiny grey frame, 19”, without pedals",
